+## #836 - Synthetos TinyG post processor (3-axis mill)
+
+**Decided:** a new built-in post, `assets/posts/tinyg.cps`, specced from the
+G-code and M-code tables of TinyG's public wiki ("Gcode Support", "Homing and
+Limits", "Flow Control and Footers", "Inch and Millimeter Units Mode") and the
+LinuxCNC G-code reference TinyG states it follows (behaviour only; the
+firmware's source is GPL and was not read). Structure from `grblhal.cps`
+(#710), the other grbl-family dialect; every golden was replayed through the
+edge-next firmware's own parser (build 450) off the board, with no refused
+line.
+
+- **No canned cycles at all.** TinyG lists G80 and nothing else of that
+  group; G81-G89 are rejected like any unlisted G code. A CYCLE record writes
+  nothing and the hole's expanded chain posts as plain moves (the Heidenhain
+  pattern), with the dwell as `G4 P<seconds>` right after the move that
+  reaches the hole's bottom (P is seconds, 0-4294, so a longer dwell is
+  refused by name). A dwell whose chain never reaches the bottom is refused,
+  not dropped. Tapping is refused by name: no G84, no spindle
+  synchronisation, and a tap cannot be plain moves.
+- **`T<n> M6` then `M0` on its own line, after the Z lift.** On TinyG M6 only
+  makes the T word the current tool and moves nothing; the halt the operator
+  needs to change and measure the tool is the program stop, queued with the
+  moves and released by the sender's cycle start. The first tool gets the same
+  stop, so the operator confirms the tool before the spindle starts. *Dropped:*
+  `M60` (the wiki lists it as "same as M0", but the common senders - cncjs,
+  Chilipeppr - react to M0/M1/M6 only); a sender-specific tool-change macro
+  (the post writes what the board itself does). Because of this M0 the post
+  is pinned by `tinyg_post.rs` for its after-operation stops instead of
+  joining `after_op.rs`'s mill list, whose tests count every M0 in a program
+  as the operator's stop.
+- **Tool numbers 1-31**, refused by name outside that range: the board keeps
+  the tool number in five bits and refuses a larger T with a status a sender
+  may not stop on.
+- **No tool length word** (no G43.1, no G49) - as #710 decided for grblHAL,
+  and for the same reason: the offset belongs to the operator or sender that
+  measures the tool at the M0, and a G49 would throw a measured length away.
+  *Dropped:* G49 in the header to clear a stale offset (SolidCraft's TinyG
+  post does this; here it would also cancel a length the sender set for this
+  job). The decision is cheap to revisit as a post option.
+- **Header `G21|G20 G17 G90 G91.1 G94 G64`**: the words a program end does
+  not reset on TinyG (the wiki's "M2, M30 Program End": units, arc-centre
+  mode and path-control mode persist), so a previous program's G90.1 or
+  G61.1 would otherwise stand. No G40 (accepted and ignored) and no G80. No
+  %, O word or N numbers; a line starting with % is a queue flush.
+- **Lengths at four decimals in either unit.** TinyG checks that an arc's
+  start and end sit at the same radius from its I J K centre; a tenth of a
+  micron keeps a rounded centre inside that check where three decimals do
+  not always. Feeds are whole mm/min (two decimals in/min).
+- **Comment cleaning** also drops `!` (feed hold), `~` (cycle start), `%`
+  (queue flush), `/` (block delete), `{` and `$` (JSON / settings when a line
+  opens with them), wherever they stand - TinyG acts on the first two even
+  inside a comment. A note opening with `msg` is led by "- " so it is not
+  echoed as an operator message. Lines are kept to 191 content bytes (the
+  receive ring has 248 usable bytes; a sender on the board's RTS marks has a
+  192-byte window); a longer line is refused by name.
+- **Z lift as grblhal.cps:** `G53 G0 Z<safe_retract>` only when the machine
+  file states it (the statement "this machine homes, and up is here");
+  otherwise `G0 Z<clearance>` in the work offset, refused by name when the
+  height is unknown or not above the stock. An unhomed TinyG has its machine
+  zero at the power-on position (`$home` 0). No G28/G30: their positions are
+  set at the machine with G28.1/G30.1, not kept across a power cycle, and
+  machine zero when unset.
+- **Control compensation refused by name** (G41/G42 are rejected by the
+  board); **go home refused by name** (see G28 above); **probing refused by
+  the engine** (no probe hooks: TinyG has G38.2 but no parameters or
+  expressions - a `#` in a line is stripped before parsing).
+- **No spindle dwell after M3.** The wiki says M3 does not wait for the
+  spindle and suggests `G4 P2` where needed. *Dropped for now:* a post option
+  for it (needs the Setup pane's post-option row); the operator's M0 before
+  the spindle start gives the same pause for a manual change. Cheap to add.
+- **Generic machine `tinyg-3axis.mch` ("TinyG 3-axis")** mirrors the grblHAL
+  generic file: a typical small router (300 x 300 x 100 mm written `-L..L`,
+  1000-24000 rpm, Flood M8 / Mist M7 - TinyG notes the two share one output
+  pin), no `safe_retract` (no homing assumed), no tool count, no power.
+- **Registered as "TinyG"** after "grblHAL" in `BUILTINS`, before the lathe
+  post; extension `.gcode`, the ending TinyG's own sample files use. The
+  synth golden drops only the tap record, as grblHAL's does.
+
+**Cost to change later:** low - a length-offset or spindle-dwell post option
+adds words without moving a golden; a 4-axis variant follows #714's path.

From 6129a9045e21ae5d2cb4d0faa8e06c6a70b0d7e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivica Safranko <safranko@msn.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:44:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] fix(post): grblHAL names a smoothing ask it cannot bound

grblHAL's core lists G61 only - no G64 P or other tolerance word - so
with per-operation smoothing (#616) on, the post now writes one
"SMOOTHING NOT WRITTEN - GRBLHAL STATES NO SMOOTHING TOLERANCE" note
per program (as Fanuc and Mazak do) instead of dropping the ask
silently; the ask resets at each section end. Pinned by
smoothing::fanuc_and_mazak_name_the_ask_once_and_write_no_unbounded_word.
Also corrects the canned-cycle comment: G85 is listed but never mapped.

Refs #710

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 assets/posts/grblhal.cps           | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 crates/app/tests/smoothing.rs      |  9 +++++----
 docs/decisions/710-grblhal-post.md |  9 +++++++++
 3 files changed, 38 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/assets/posts/grblhal.cps b/assets/posts/grblhal.cps
index b16d6b386..3599b9830 100644
--- a/assets/posts/grblhal.cps
+++ b/assets/posts/grblhal.cps
@@ -39,6 +39,9 @@ var coolantOp = "";        // the section's OperationName, for refusals (#150)
 var sectionOpen = false;   // preamble written (a legacy .cl carries no SECTION)
 var orgX = 0, orgY = 0, orgZ = 0; // the WCS slot origin (OriginX/Y/Z PARAMs)
 var inch = false;          // the machine is programmed in inches (onOpen)
+var smoothTol = 0;         // #616: the section's PARAM Smoothing, mm (0: none asked)
+var smoothMode = "";       // #616: "finish" or "rough"
+var smoothNamed = false;   // the not-written note, once per program
 
 // ------------------------------------------------------------ helpers
 // The stream speaks mm and mm/min. An inch machine gets every length and
@@ -270,6 +273,8 @@ function onParameter(name, value) {
   if (name === "OperationName") coolantOp = String(value || "");
   if (name === "Coolant") { coolantAsk = String(value || "flood"); return; }
   if (name === "AfterOperation") { afterAsk = String(value || ""); return; }
+  if (name === "Smoothing") { smoothTol = Number(value) || 0; return; }
+  if (name === "SmoothingMode") { smoothMode = String(value || ""); return; }
   if (name === "WorkOffset" && value) wcsWord = String(value);
   else if (name === "OriginX" && has(value)) orgX = Number(value);
   else if (name === "OriginY" && has(value)) orgY = Number(value);
@@ -292,6 +297,20 @@ function onToolChange(number, name) {
   toolWait = true;
 }
 
+// #616: per-operation smoothing. grblHAL's core states path control
+// G61 (exact path) only - no G64 P and no other word that bounds the
+// deviation by a tolerance - so the ask is named once per program and
+// nothing is written: never an unbounded blending word.
+function smoothOn() {
+  if (!(smoothTol > 0) || smoothNamed) return;
+  note("SMOOTHING NOT WRITTEN - GRBLHAL STATES NO SMOOTHING TOLERANCE");
+  smoothNamed = true;
+}
+function smoothOff() {  // the next section states its own ask
+  smoothTol = 0;
+  smoothMode = "";
+}
+
 // The preamble closes over everything a raw motion line needs to be a
 // legal program: plane, offset, tool, spindle, coolant. Before a tool
 // change Z goes straight up in machine coordinates; then `T<n> M6` stands
@@ -318,6 +337,7 @@ function startPreamble() {
   spindleWait = false;
   coolant = touchProbe ? "" : coolantFor(coolantAsk);
   if (coolant) block([coolant]);
+  smoothOn();
 }
 
 // The op's after-action (#110), written once its spindle has stopped:
@@ -341,6 +361,7 @@ function endPreamble() {
   if (!sectionOpen) return;
   restorePlane();            // the plane never leaks past its section
   sectionOpen = false;
+  smoothOff();
   if (inCycle) block(["G80"]);
   inCycle = false;
   if (coolant) block(["M9"]);
@@ -410,7 +431,9 @@ function onCircular() {
 }
 
 // ------------------------------------------------------- canned cycles
-// grblHAL's core lists G73, G81, G82, G83, G85, G86, G89 with G98/G99.
+// grblHAL's core lists G73, G81, G82, G83, G85, G86, G89 with G98/G99;
+// this post writes all of them but G85 (no CamCraft cycle asks for a
+// feed-out bore, so it is never mapped).
 // One block per hole, holes of an unchanged cycle continuing modally
 // with bare X Y lines. The dwell P is in SECONDS, as in LinuxCNC (not
 // the milliseconds Fanuc-family controls read). G84 is not in the list
diff --git a/crates/app/tests/smoothing.rs b/crates/app/tests/smoothing.rs
index 49ebd5f50..70c91ab95 100644
--- a/crates/app/tests/smoothing.rs
+++ b/crates/app/tests/smoothing.rs
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 //! at the section's end.
 //!
 //! Gate map (#616): covers app::smoothing (of, rough_tol), post::dump
-//! (the Smoothing PARAMs), the six mill posts' smoothOn/smoothOff.
+//! (the Smoothing PARAMs), the mill posts' smoothOn/smoothOff (grblHAL's #710 note included).
 //! Provenance: our own fixtures; each dialect's words from its public
 //! programming documentation (see the posts).
 
@@ -100,9 +100,10 @@ fn each_dialect_writes_its_words_and_undoes_them_at_the_section_end() {
 
 #[test]
 fn fanuc_and_mazak_name_the_ask_once_and_write_no_unbounded_word() {
-    // Fanuc's G5.1 states no tolerance (review of #635) and Mazak has no
-    // stated form: the ask is named, never written loose.
-    for name in ["Fanuc", "Mazak"] {
+    // Fanuc's G5.1 states no tolerance (review of #635), Mazak has no
+    // stated form and grblHAL lists G61 only (#710): the ask is named,
+    // never written loose.
+    for name in ["Fanuc", "Mazak", "grblHAL"] {
         let prog = program(name, FINISH);
         assert_eq!(lines_with(&prog, "SMOOTHING NOT WRITTEN").len(), 1, "{name}:\n{prog}");
         assert!(!prog.contains("G5.1 Q"), "{name}: no unbounded G5.1:\n{prog}");
diff --git a/docs/decisions/710-grblhal-post.md b/docs/decisions/710-grblhal-post.md
index 2b29d85d2..dea70b8c2 100644
--- a/docs/decisions/710-grblhal-post.md
+++ b/docs/decisions/710-grblhal-post.md
@@ -62,6 +62,15 @@ G-code list in grblHAL's public core README and the LinuxCNC G-code reference
 - **End units option** (`EndUnits`) is read by the script, but the Setup
   pane's end-units row still shows only for Tormach; widening it is UI
   work left out of this PR.
+- **Per-operation smoothing (#616) is named, not written** (review of
+  PR #715). grblHAL's core lists G61 (exact path) only - no G64 P and no
+  other word bounds the deviation by a tolerance. With smoothing on, the
+  program carries one `(SMOOTHING NOT WRITTEN - GRBLHAL STATES NO
+  SMOOTHING TOLERANCE)` note, the way Fanuc and Mazak name an ask they
+  cannot bound; the ask resets at each section end. Dropped: writing G64
+  without P (unbounded blending - worse than none), and staying silent
+  (the user's ask would vanish). Pinned by
+  `smoothing::fanuc_and_mazak_name_the_ask_once_and_write_no_unbounded_word`.
 
 **Cost to change later:** low - a post option for the length offset or for G30
 before M6 adds words without moving any existing golden.

