From 7468f847b2b4e0767dd3b4223e7f60ca54554b93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Riley Porter <rileyporter@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:09:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] fix(post): make TinyG tool changes and motion output safe

Stop outputs explicitly before manual tool changes, restore modal state
and Z clearance after M0, and seat the first cut at its safe start.
Refuse rounded-zero feeds and ambiguous tiny arcs, split XY full turns,
and bound non-XY chord output for older-controller compatibility.
Add optional spindle dwell, name smoothing requests, and include the
recorded TinyG post suite and updated regression evidence.

Refs #836

Co-Authored-By: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
